{"sourceSha256": "a51977ad103d324faca2e3879ade08c5d447edc11869b7d39be57ea1bada6fb9", "text": "11/02/2019\n\nDr Christine Hodges\n2 Hill Forest Road\nNewtown\n\nDear Dr Hodges,\nRe: Mr John Aloisius\n\nI am writing to discharge Mr Aloisius from our Emergency Department back into\nyour care. Your further management would be highly appreciated.\n\nOn 01/02/2019, Mr Aloisius presented complaining of tuberculosis symptoms.\nExamination revealed cachexia and scattered rales. A chest x-ray result showed\napical infiltrates, and a sputum acid-fast stain and a mycobacterial culture\nconfirmed the diagnosis of tuberculosis. As a result, he was placed in respiratory   Deleted: on\nisolation and tuberculosis medications were started, including isoniazid 5mg/kg\nfour times daily, rifampin 10 mg/kg one time per day, pyrazinamide 15-30             Commented [RB1]: This can be expressed as ‘once’.\nmg/kg four times a day, ethambutol 2.8g twice weekly and vitamin B-6 50 mg\nonce daily.\n\nToday, Mr Aloisius’s sputum acid-fast stain was negative indicating good\nprogress. Regarding his discharge plan, the drug regimen with vitamin B-6 will\ncontinue for four months. However, pyrazinamide and ethambutol will be ceased\nafter two months. He requires monitoring of his medication compliance,               Deleted: ensuring\nreduction of the regimen above to 2-3 times a week after two weeks of the initial    Commented [RB2]: Above is an adverb, not an\ndose, toxicity monitoring, baseline and periodic serum uric acid assessments,        adjective. Thus, it is not used before nouns.\nperiodic visual acuity and red-green color perception tests.                         Deleted: above\n\n\nIn light of the information above, your continuous care and follow-up of Mr\nAloisius’s condition would be greatly valued. If you require any further\nclarification, please do not hesitate to get in contact.                             Commented [RB3]: Possibly a little informal. Try:\n                                                                                     …hesitate to contact me.\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor\n\n                             Writing Feedback:\n   Criteria         Needs work        Satisfactory                 Strong\n Purpose                                                ✓\n Content                                                     ✓\n\n Conciseness                                                 ✓\n & Clarity\n Genre &                                               ✓\n Style\n Organisation                                          ✓\n & Layout\n\n Language\n\f\n✓\nOverall\nComments\n             Hawazen\n             The purpose has been established sufficiently and the content is\n             relevant and extended, so well done. Ideally, look to establish the\n             purpose clearly in the introduction which will then leave the\n             conclusion as a more generic statement. Linguistically, error free\n             sentences are evident despite some scattered errors with word\n             order and prepositions. Use the live grammar classes and online\n             resources on the OET online website to assist with reviewing these\n             items. If you require further clarification, please feel free to contact\n             me.\n\n             Focus Areas:\n                • Prepositions\n\n\n\n\nOverall Grade: B (around 360)", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "11/02/2019\n\nDr Christine Hodges\n2 Hill Forest Road\nNewtown\n\nDear Dr Hodges,\nRe: Mr John Aloisius\n\nI am writing to discharge Mr Aloisius from our Emergency Department back into\nyour care. Your further management would be highly appreciated.\n\nOn 01/02/2019, Mr Aloisius presented complaining of tuberculosis symptoms.\nExamination revealed cachexia and scattered rales. A chest x-ray result showed\napical infiltrates, and a sputum acid-fast stain and a mycobacterial culture\nconfirmed the diagnosis of tuberculosis. As a result, he was placed in respiratory  